Hello.

I am having issues with embedding google motion charts inside html_document, generated by knitr. Here's a small example:

```{r, results='asis'}
library('googleVis')
motion <- gvisMotionChart(data = Fruits, idvar = 'Fruit', timevar = 'Year',
                          xvar = 'Sales', yvar = 'Expenses')
print(motion, 'chart')

line <- gvisLineChart(data = Fruits, xvar = 'Sales', yvar = 'Expenses')
print(line, 'chart')
```

The line chart is displaying just fine. The motion chart is showing blank.
Running plot(motion) displays motion chart inside browser just fine, so this is not browser issue (tested output in FF, Chrome, IE).
