As far as I can recall, knitr does not touch the random seed, and this
can be verified by a minimal Rnw document, e.g.

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
<<>>=
str(.Random.seed)
@
\end{document}

You should see an error ".Random.seed not found".

Anyway, I'm glad that you came up with a fix, and we will see if there
are any further problems. Thanks!

